```
:::
:::


1. A common mistake is to assume that percentage calculations should be based on the entire dataframe. Here, percentages are calculated only after filtering for the target libraries, Banyo and Hamilton.

### Question Three

(3) **Create a bar chart showing the five most popular checked-out items.**

Some rows in the *Item* column contain null values. Since null values should not be counted among the most popular items, they must be filtered out before aggregation.

::: {#cf80c05a .cell execution_count=11}
``` {.python .cell-code}
from bokeh.models import NumeralTickFormatter

(library_checkouts
.filter(pl.col('Item').is_not_null())
.group_by('Item').len()
.top_k(5, by='len') # <1>
.hvplot.barh(x='Item', y='len',
            xlabel='', ylabel='')
.opts(title='Top 5 most popular items checked-out',
    xformatter=NumeralTickFormatter(format='0a')) # <2>
)
```

