### Question Nine

(9) **Create a single column dataframe that shows a numbered list of Cal Newport books. The first row should be the full author name and book titles should be in the subsequent rows.**

This question relies on intermediate variables. First, we extract all books written by Cal Newport and store them in a variable named *cn_books*.

::: {#a3f17635 .cell execution_count=17}
``` {.python .cell-code}
cn_books = (library_checkouts
 .filter(pl.col('Title').is_not_null(), # <1>
         pl.col('Author').str.contains('Newport, Cal'))
 .with_columns(pl.col('Author').str.strip_chars(','),
               pl.col('Title').str.strip_chars(' /'))
 .with_columns(pl.col('Title').str.replace('FASTBACK - ',''), # <2>
               pl.col('Author').str.split(', ').list.reverse().list.join(' ')) # <3>
 .select('Title','Author')
 .with_columns(pl.col('Title').str.replace('sm on','sm : on')) # <4>
 .unique('Title')
 )
cn_books
```

