1. Omitting this line would introduce a null value into the result set.
2. Some titles appear to be unique only because they include the text "FASTBACK". Removing this text ensures that identical titles are treated as the same book.
3. This reverses the author name so it appears as first name followed by last name.
4. One title includes a colon before the subtitle while another does not. This standardization ensures both are treated as the same book.

Now we construct the final output.

```{.python}
(cn_books
 .select('Author')
 .head(1)
 .vstack(cn_books
 .select(pl.col('Title').sort())
 .rename(dict(Title='Author'))) # <1>
 .with_columns(pl.when(pl.int_range(pl.len()) > 0) # <2>
               .then(pl.format('{}. {}', pl.int_range(pl.len()), pl.col('Author')))
               .otherwise(pl.col('Author'))
               .alias('Author'))
 )
```

